  "chunks": [
    {
      "chunk_type": "isnad",
      "arabic_text": "مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ يَحْيَى عَنْ أَحْمَدَ بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ عَنْ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ سِنَانٍ عَنِ ابْنِ مُسْكَانَ عَنِ الْحَلَبِيِّ أَنَّهُ سَأَلَ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام )",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Muhammad ibn Yahya, from Ahmad ibn Muhammad, from Muhammad ibn Sinan, from Ibn Muskan, from Al-Halby, that he asked Abu Abdillah (peace be upon him)"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "عَنْ صَلَاةِ النَّافِلَةِ عَلَى الْبَعِيرِ وَ الدَّابَّةِ فَقَالَ نَعَمْ حَيْثُمَا كُنْتَ مُتَوَجِّهاً قَالَ فَقُلْتُ عَلَى الْبَعِيرِ وَ الدَّابَّةِ قَالَ نَعَمْ حَيْثُمَا كُنْتَ مُتَوَجِّهاً قُلْتُ أَسْتَقْبِلُ الْقِبْلَةَ إِذَا أَرَدْتُ التَّكْبِيرَ قَالَ لَا وَ لَكِنْ تُكَبِّرُ حَيْثُمَا كُنْتَ مُتَوَجِّهاً وَ كَذَلِكَ فَعَلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ( صلى الله عليه وآله )",
      "translations": {
        "en": "about the optional prayer upon the camel and the riding animal, so he (peace be upon him) said: 'Yes, wherever you are facing.' I said, 'Upon the camel and the riding animal?' He (peace be upon him) said: 'Yes, wherever you are facing.' I said, 'Do I face the Qiblah when I intend to say Takbir?' He (peace be upon him) said: 'No, but you say Takbir wherever you are facing, and that is what the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) did.'"
      }
    }
  ],
  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "summary": "This hadith establishes the legal ruling for performing voluntary prayer while riding an animal during travel. It clarifies that one does not need to face the Qiblah specifically when initiating the prayer (Takbir), but rather prays in the direction the animal is facing, following the practice of the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family).",
      "seo_question": "How should one perform voluntary prayer while riding a camel or animal during travel?",
      "key_terms": {
        "صَلَاةُ النَّافِلَةِ": "Optional/Voluntary prayer",
        "عَلَى الْبَعِيرِ": "Upon the camel (prayer while riding)",
        "الدَّابَّةِ": "The riding animal/beast",
        "الْقِبْلَةَ": "The Qiblah (direction of prayer)",
        "التَّكْبِيرَ": "The Takbir (saying Allahu Akbar to start prayer)",
        "ر initiate prayer)"
